    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Gods And Zeros is the long-awaited debut album from Panixphere, a trio featuring Bic Hayes, Jon Poole, and Bob Leith. Released by ATE Music, it distills the band’s early live-project spirit into 13 original tracks: frantic, irreverent rock shaped by punk urgency, skewed rhythms, angular guitar, and flashes of ska-like energy. The performances retain a deliberately unruly edge, but the arrangements are focused enough to give the album a strong sense of momentum and identity.\n\nThe record also carries considerable significance for followers of the Ring and Cardiacs orbit. “Perfic,” associated with Jon Poole and later transformed into “Angleworm Angel” for Cardiacs’ Sing to God, connects the album to that wider musical history, while songs such as “Pandy” and “More Money Than God” highlight Bic Hayes’s eccentric, hook-conscious songwriting. Contemporary reception emphasized the album’s “frantic feast” of ideas and its ability to recapture the urgent magic of the musicians’ early work, making Gods And Zeros both an archival release and a vivid standalone rock album.",
